<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#star-catalogue">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Star catalogue</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as star catalogues</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A star catalogue is a list of stars with their positions and brightness. The Timurid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulugh-beg">Ulugh Beg</a>'s observatory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> produced star catalogues of high accuracy. They were used by European astronomers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/star-catalogue.jpg" alt="Star catalogue" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Heweliusz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perseus_-_Prodromus_astronomiae_1690_(5590393).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
